        "returncode": 0,
        "stdout": "Courier Relay protocol 1 delivery identity and receipt acceptance contract. Applies to protocol \"1\", initially current in trial-74m. Source: vendor/protocol-1.md, designated as the provider contract by issue trial-74m; this is provider-specified behavior, not an inferred product approval.\n\nA delivery identity is the pair (account_id, delivery_id). The same delivery_id under another account identifies a separate delivery. This follows the provider delivery-ID allocation guarantee; account attribution alone does not change that guarantee. Exactly one receipt is accepted per identity: choose earliest occurred_at as a UTC instant, breaking equal-instant ties by smallest record_id in Unicode code-point order. All others for that identity are duplicates. Accepted receipts retain every original field, timestamp spelling, and payload, and are presented in original input order. Those selection and presentation rules remain part of the contract even though count does not expose receipts.\n\nIssue trial-74m specifies receipts with exactly record_id, account_id, delivery_id, occurred_at, payload; nonempty string IDs, request-unique record_id, string payload; RFC3339 timestamps with seconds, no fractions, Z or numeric offset, dates 2020–2099. Compare UTC instants even across date boundaries. Requests are complete independent sets with no cross-invocation persistence; lists may be empty. This issue supplies at most one account per request, but that restriction does not narrow the provider identity definition.\n\nOmitted protocol chooses current; explicitly supported versions remain supported after a current-version change. Protocol 1 count returns exactly protocol (\"1\"), accepted_count, duplicate_count. Derived count rule: accepted_count equals distinct identity pairs; duplicate_count equals total receipts minus accepted_count. Winner selection does not affect these totals.\n\nValidation in trial-74m: python3 test_public.py --cases public_tests/count_1.json passed both cases; python3 -m unittest discover -s tests passed 4 tests, including CLI duplicate counting with changed payloads, offset timestamps, tied instants, reversed input, explicit/default protocol, empty default input, ping and unknown command. These count tests do not validate winner selection or accepted-receipt presentation.\n",
